# LF in every working tree, on every platform. Without this a Windows checkout gets CRLF, and every
# multi-line string literal in the Scala sources then carries "\r\n": generated text (issue templates,
# the payload-layout region) stops matching what the tests expect, although it prints identically.
# Found by the v0.10.3 Windows release build. There are no .bat/.cmd/.ps1 files that would need CRLF.
* text=auto eol=lf
